EPRED (1 instances; assumes: take = filter)
  statement: size(F) > i implies predF(F[i]) for filtered F (exactly-encodable conjuncts of predF)
IDOM (1 instances; assumes: ORD + SUB)
  statement: pt(F[i]) <= pt(P[i]) for filtered F of P
PRES (2 instances; assumes: none)
  statement: 0 <= defined(q) <= 1 for every presence indicator
PDEF (2 instances; assumes: none)
  statement: defined(C[i].x) >= 1 => size(C) > i (front index i; back index -k gives size(C) >= k)
EPRES (1 instances; assumes: take = filter)
  statement: size(F) > i => defined(F[i].x) >= 1, for a filtered F whose filter predicate is FALSE on every element lacking x

